WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.890
Week 8: Family, Description, and Possession. describe people and relationships express possession identify a person precisely

2
00:00:08.890 --> 00:00:17.311
Cultural lens. Extended family, chosen family, household diversity, and respectful relationship vocabulary.

3
00:00:17.311 --> 00:00:29.382
Avoid the single-story trap. Treat country, region, age, relationship, and setting as variables. Describe the evidence you have without turning one example into a universal rule.

4
00:00:29.382 --> 00:00:41.240
Language variation. Recognize regional choices and ask what a form means locally. Use the neutral course model for production until the situation gives you a reason to adapt.

5
00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:50.239
Reflection. Compare this context with one you know. Name one similarity, one difference, and one question that would prevent an assumption.

6
00:00:50.239 --> 00:01:19.953
Model language. Muchas familias son extendidas. — Many families are extended. Algunas personas tienen una familia elegida. — Some people have a chosen family. Cada hogar es diferente. — Every household is different. El respeto no depende de la estructura familiar. — Respect doesn't depend on family structure. Es importante describir las relaciones con precisión. — It's important to describe relationships precisely.

7
00:01:19.953 --> 00:01:29.873
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
